<body>
    <h1>Copy of Maximus Master Release Documentation and Guidelines</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"1427ce26e73e"><strong>Purpose:</strong> This page defines th=
e standard master release process for Maximus products and shared services.=
 It covers scope, release principles, ownership, release flow, mandatory ga=
tes, evidence requirements, rollback expectations, deployment controls, and=
 environment deployment references.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"dd8ea3ec1721"><strong>Applies to:</strong> All Maximus produ=
cts and shared services included in a master release train. No product may =
bypass shared quality, security, approval, or rollback requirements.</p>
</div>
</div>
